        <body>
            <div xml:id="d97">

                <pb facs="0134" n="100" sameAs="frus:frus1897/pg100"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Denby to Mr. Sherman.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Pekin</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1897-03-16"><hi rendition="#italic">March 16, 1897</hi></date>.
                        (Received April 26.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 2713.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: In my dispatch No. 2705, of the 11th
                    instant, I transmitted a copy of a communication which was sent by me to the
                    Tsung-li Yamên, demanding the dismissal from office of the magistrate, Liu
                    Yan-Kwang, whom the governor of Kiangsu had promised should be dismissed on
                    account of his neglect of duty at the time of the occurrence of the riot at
                    Kiang Yin.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to inclose a translation of the Yamên’s answer, from which it
                    will be seen that the matter has been referred to the governor for his report
                    thereon.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Charles Denby.</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d97-a1.xml" xpointer="d97-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
